; Sprites: spiky post, left and right (8 frames)
;
; Eight 16x16 sprites of 32 bytes, 16 pixel rows of 2 bytes each (left byte, right byte; bit 7 = leftmost pixel). Sprite
; F of the page is at $B500+32*F. Entity definitions (#R$A000) name the page in byte +5 and pick F from the animation
; phase, the direction and the slot data. The sprites are drawn with #R$9456 (#R$91BE) and have no colour of their own:
; ink and bright come from the entity definition. Narrow upright serrated shapes with a few loose pixels; most of the
; picture is in the left byte column and frames 0 and 4 are only a small blob. Frames 0-3 are used while moving left,
; 4-7 while moving right (bit 7 of entity byte +0). Used by entity definitions $34 $35 $58 $6F in rooms $03 $07 $0D $1E
; $31 $33 $38 $3B.
@label=SpritesSpikyPosts
b$B500 DEFB $00,$00 ; frame 0: spiky post (left), frame 0, small blob
